  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAn upper level trough remains over the the northeast CONUS and\neastern Great Lakes region this afternoon. A cold northerly \nwill continue over the eastern Great Lakes today through early \nSunday. Scattered lake effect rain showers, mixing with wet snow\nat times, will continue across the Snowbelt of northeast Ohio \nand northwest Pennsylvania this afternoon through early Sunday. \nLittle to no accumulation is expected with the wet snow. Drier \nair will start to move into the area later on Sunday which will \nshut off the lake effect precip. High temperatures today and \nSunday will be in the 40s. Tonight's low temperatures will be \nin the lower to middle 30s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nHigh pressure will build over the region early next week and\nlinger through the end of the week. Mostly quiet and dry weather\nis in the forecast through much of the upcoming week. High\ntemperatures will start out seasonable in the upper 40s to lower\n50s. By the middle and end of the week, high temperatures will\nbe above average in the upper 50s to lower 60s.",
